  "@type": "Process",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Fire detection and suppression for crewed spacecraft: smoke particulate detectors (ionisation and photoelectric) in cabin air ducts, portable and fixed CO2 and water-mist extinguishers, flame-retardant material selection, and post-fire atmosphere cleanup. Microgravity flame behaviour differs markedly from terrestrial flames — flames are spherical, spread slower along solid fuel, and produce more smoke particulate, requiring dedicated detector placement and response procedures.",
  "early_win": false,
